(11,'KEEP',[II],'theory','Equal normal-incidence transmission for two elastic polarizations','Normal incidence on planar layers decouples longitudinal and shear polarization into scalar waves. Wave impedance and displacement/traction matching determine the equality condition in terms of material densities and wave speeds; no finite-solid tensor deformation is requested.'),
(12,'KEEP',[I,II],'numerical','Pressure and freely suspended box motion under spherical infrasound','Sound intensity/pressure, ordinary acoustic waves and pressure force differences drive a rigid mass. Wavelength/box/distance scales control cancellation and stationary response. Dimensions, mass and damping remain estimate assumptions.'),
(13,'KEEP',[III,II],'experimental','Tube-and-box acoustic trap design and placement','Air compressibility and the moving air column form a conventional Helmholtz oscillator. Tuning its resonance and placing it at pressure antinodes uses gas law, oscillations and room waves. Real dissipation must be included as an ordinary loss estimate.'),
