(22,'KEEP',[I,VII],'experimental','Rolling two-magnet homopolar motor','The N-N pole orientation, coatings, current strips and voltage signs are shown. Lorentz force/current torque, contact reaction and electromagnetic momentum account for rolling and conservation with the external circuit/table. No exotic magnetic material law is needed.'),
(23,'KEEP',[VI],'theory','Conductor polarization self-energy and electrostatic reciprocity','Induced sphere surface charges, field/self/interacting energy and dipole forces are ordinary electrostatics. Allowing source/induced charge readjustment and correct polarization energy resolves the apparent inconsistency.'),
(24,'KEEP',[I,VII],'numerical','Transfer matrices of magnetic accelerator focusing','The paraxial variables/design path and transfer convention are explicit, and the source explicitly permits nonrelativistic derivation with momentum replacement. Lorentz-force trajectories give drifts, quadrupoles and bends; products and momentum dependence give focus/chromatic error without a Lorentz transformation.'),
(25,'KEEP',[IV,VI],'numerical','Joule heating and travelling thermal quench under stated material rules','Temperature-dependent copper resistance and piecewise constant superconducting-state resistance/thermal properties are supplied. Joule energy balance and ordinary Fourier heat conduction produce the travelling thermal front. No microscopic superconductivity theory is needed.'),
(26,'KEEP',[IV,XI],'theory','Two-star blackbody temperatures using supplied flux and entropy ratio','Geometry and blackbody flux constrain fourth powers of temperatures. Radiation energy/pressure thermodynamics gives entropy proportional to volume*T^3, so the supplied ratio closes the two-temperature equations. Exotic setting adds no new stellar theory.'),
(27,'BORDERLINE',[I],'theory','Trajectory and growth of a stipulated classical microscopic black hole','The source explicitly restricts the object to classical gravity, so Newtonian trajectory work is accessible. It does not specify an absorption radius/capture/energy-loss rule needed for mass growth; importing a horizon or accretion law would add unsupplied physics. Whole-task interpretation is unresolved.'),
(28,'REJECT',[],'theory','Force-dependent polymerization through an unsupplied thermal ratchet model','Zero-force attachment/detachment rates and monomer size are supplied, but obstacle-gap statistics, thermal fluctuations and the force dependence of monomer availability are not. A Brownian-ratchet or alternative force-dependent kinetic law is the central missing model for both requested results.'),
